-- title:
--   pp. 3–4, 9–11, 17–18, 32–34 — delayed marked Galton–Watson tree, signals, recursions (1)/(8) and (9), limiting opinions 𝓜*, 𝓡*, moments ρ₁, ρ₂, 𝓨, 𝓥, p_m and the Lemma 9 coefficients
-- statement:
--   This file fixes the probabilistic model of Sections 5 and 5.4 and of the appendix of Fraiman, Lin and Olvera-Cravioto, together with every derived quantity used by Proposition 6, (15), Theorem 8, Remark 10.2 and Lemma 9.
--
--   **The tree.** Nodes are labelled by finite words $\mathbf i=(i_1,\dots,i_k)$ (Ulam–Harris labels), the root being the empty word $\varnothing$. Every label carries a mark $\mathcal X_{\mathbf i}$ in a measurable space $M$; the recursion reads off a mark only its in-degree $\mathcal N_{\mathbf i}\in\mathbb N$, its neighbour weights $\mathcal C_{(\mathbf i,1)},\mathcal C_{(\mathbf i,2)},\dots\in[0,1]$, and its internal opinion $\mathcal Q_{\mathbf i}\in[-1,1]$. The parameters satisfy $c\in[0,1)$, $d\in(0,1]$, $c+d\le 1$, and the weights of a node with $\mathcal N_{\mathbf i}\ge 1$ sum to $c$. The tree is a **delayed marked Galton–Watson tree**: the marks $\{\mathcal X_{\mathbf i}\}$ are independent, and $\{\mathcal X_{\mathbf i}:\mathbf i\neq\varnothing\}$ are identically distributed (the root may have a different law).
--
--   **Signals.** The media signals are $\mathcal Z_{\mathbf i}^{(k)}=\zeta(\mathcal X_{\mathbf i},U_{\mathbf i}^{(k)})\in[-1,1]$, $k\ge 0$, where $\{U_{\mathbf i}^{(k)}\}$ are i.i.d. uniform on $[0,1]$ and independent of the marks. The Section 5.1 external signal is
--   $$\mathcal W_{\mathbf i}^{(k)} = d\,\mathcal Z_{\mathbf i}^{(k)} + \mathcal Q_{\mathbf i}\Big(c-\sum_{j=1}^{\mathcal N_{\mathbf i}}\mathcal C_{(\mathbf i,j)}\Big).$$
--   The same representation $\xi(\mathcal X_{\mathbf i},U_{\mathbf i}^{(k)})$ with a general measurable $\xi$ gives the general signals of the appendix.
--
--   **Recursions and limiting opinions.** For weights $w$, degrees $n$ and a self-weight $\lambda$, the tree operator is $(\Delta f)(\mathbf i)=\sum_{j=1}^{n_{\mathbf i}} w_{(\mathbf i,j)}f(\mathbf i,j)+\lambda f(\mathbf i)$. The limiting opinion of node $\mathbf i$ is the series $\sum_{s\ge0}(\Delta^s\mathcal W^{(s)})(\mathbf i)$, and the opinion at time $k$ started from $\mathcal R^{(0)}\equiv 0$ is $\sum_{r<k}(\Delta^r\mathcal W^{(k-1-r)})(\mathbf i)$. The general recursion (8) uses the weights $\mathcal C$ and $\lambda=1-c-d$; its root opinion is $\mathcal M^*$. The no-memory recursion (9) uses the weights $\mathcal C/(c+d)$, $\lambda=0$ and the signals $\mathcal W/(c+d)$; its root opinion is $\mathcal R^*$.
--
--   **Moments.** $\rho_1^*=E[\sum_{i=1}^{\mathcal N_\varnothing}\mathcal C_i]$, $\rho_1=E[\sum_{i=1}^{\mathcal N_1}\mathcal C_{(1,i)}]$, $\rho_2^*=E[\sum_{i=1}^{\mathcal N_\varnothing}\mathcal C_i^2]$, $\rho_2=E[\sum_{i=1}^{\mathcal N_1}\mathcal C_{(1,i)}^2]$; $\mathcal Y_{\mathbf i}=E[\mathcal W_{\mathbf i}^{(0)}\mid\mathcal X_{\mathbf i}]$ and $\mathcal V_{\mathbf i}=\mathrm{Var}(\mathcal W_{\mathbf i}^{(0)}\mid\mathcal X_{\mathbf i})$. Further,
--   $$p_m=\sum_{s=0}^\infty\binom{s+m}{s}^2(1-c-d)^{2s}(c+d)^{2(m+1)},\qquad a_{l,s}=\binom{s}{l}(1-c-d)^{s-l},$$
--   the expectation of $g(T)$ for $T$ Geometric on $\{0,1,2,\dots\}$ with success probability $1-\rho$ is the series $\sum_k\rho^k(1-\rho)g(k)$, and $S_{k,m}$, $U_{k,m}$, $T_{k,m}$ are the coefficients of Lemma 9.
--
--   These objects are shared by every statement of the mission.
--
--   **Formalization Note.** Labels are `List ℕ` with 0-based child indices: the paper's $r$-th neighbour of $\mathbf i$ is `i ++ [r-1]`, and the paper's node $1$ is `[0]`. Every label carries a mark and signals, also outside the tree; `treeOp` follows only children $j<\mathcal N_{\mathbf i}$, so such labels are never reached from a node of the tree. The signal law is encoded by a quantile representation $\zeta(x,U)$ with i.i.d. uniforms independent of the marks: this is equivalent in law to "conditionally i.i.d. given $\mathcal X_{\mathbf i}=x$ with law $\nu(x)$" (take $\zeta(x,\cdot)$ the quantile function of $\nu(x)$), the device the paper uses on p. 25, and every statement of the mission concerns laws only. Since $|\Delta^s f|\le(1-d)^s\sup|f|$ for (8) and $\le(c/(c+d))^s\sup|f|$ for (9), every opinion series is absolutely summable under the standing assumptions; `nodeOpinion` is the series, not a junk value. $E$ is the Bochner integral, Var is `ProbabilityTheory.variance`, Cov is `ProbabilityTheory.covariance`, and conditional moments are `condExp`/`condVar` with respect to the $\sigma$-algebra generated by $\mathcal X_{\mathbf i}$ (a.e.-defined functions). `aCoef` uses natural-number subtraction $s-l$ and is only evaluated at $l\le s$.
-- source:
--   Fraiman, Lin and Olvera-Cravioto, Opinion dynamics on directed complex networks, arXiv:2209.00969v2, pp. 3–4 (1), p. 9–11 §§5, 5.1, pp. 17–18 (8)–(9), pp. 32–34 Theorem 8 and Lemma 9

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_DirectedOpinion_NoMemory_Setting

namespace DirectedOpinion.Memory
open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory Set

variable {Ω M : Type*} [MeasurableSpace Ω] [MeasurableSpace M]

/-- Limiting opinion of node `i`: Σ_{s ≥ 0} (Δ^s 𝓦^(s))(i). `rootOpinion = nodeOpinion · [] `. -/
noncomputable def nodeOpinion (n : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ) (w : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ → ℝ) (lam : ℝ)
    (sig : ℕ → DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℝ) (i : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label) : ℝ :=
  ∑' s : ℕ, ((DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.treeOp n w lam)^[s] (sig s)) i

/-- Opinions at time `k` started from 𝓡^(0) ≡ 0: 𝓡^(k) = Σ_{r < k} Δ^r 𝓦^(k−1−r), i.e. the
recursion 𝓡^(k+1) = Δ𝓡^(k) + 𝓦^(k) iterated `k` times from the zero vector. -/
noncomputable def fwdOpinion (n : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ) (w : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ → ℝ) (lam : ℝ)
    (sig : ℕ → DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℝ) (k : ℕ) (i : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label) : ℝ :=
  ∑ r ∈ Finset.range k, ((DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.treeOp n w lam)^[r] (sig (k - 1 - r))) i

/-- p_m = Σ_{s ≥ 0} binom(s + m, s)² (1 − c − d)^{2s} (c + d)^{2(m+1)} (Theorem 8, p. 33). -/
noncomputable def pT (c d : ℝ) (m : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ∑' s : ℕ, ((s + m).choose s : ℝ) ^ 2 * (1 - c - d) ^ (2 * s) * (c + d) ^ (2 * (m + 1))

/-- E[g(T)] for T Geometric on {0, 1, 2, …} with success probability 1 − ρ, i.e.
P(T = k) = ρ^k (1 − ρ): the series Σ_k ρ^k (1 − ρ) g(k). -/
noncomputable def geomExp (ρ : ℝ) (g : ℕ → ℝ) : ℝ :=
  ∑' k : ℕ, ρ ^ k * (1 - ρ) * g k

/-- S_{k,m} = Σ_{s=1}^k Σ_{l=1}^s a_{l+m,s+m} ρ₁^{l−1} (Lemma 9, p. 34). -/
noncomputable def Scoef (c d ρ₁ : ℝ) (k m : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ s ∈ Finset.Icc 1 k, ∑ l ∈ Finset.Icc 1 s, DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.aCoef c d (l + m) (s + m) * ρ₁ ^ (l - 1)

/-- U_{k,m} = Σ_{s=0}^k a_{m,s+m} (Lemma 9, p. 34). -/
noncomputable def Ucoef (c d : ℝ) (k m : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ s ∈ Finset.range (k + 1), DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.aCoef c d m (s + m)

/-- T_{k,m} = Σ_{s=0}^k a²_{m,s+m} (Lemma 9, p. 34). -/
noncomputable def Tcoef (c d : ℝ) (k m : ℕ) : ℝ :=
  ∑ s ∈ Finset.range (k + 1), DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.aCoef c d m (s + m) ^ 2

/-- In-degrees of the tree at the outcome ω: i ↦ 𝓝_i. -/
def nAt (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) (ω : Ω) : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ :=
  fun i => mk.N (X i ω)

/-- Weights of the tree at the outcome ω: (i, j) ↦ 𝓒_(i,j+1). -/
def wAt (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) (ω : Ω) : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ → ℝ :=
  fun i j => mk.C (X i ω) j

/-- Sum of the weights of node `i`: Σ_{j ≤ 𝓝_i} 𝓒_(i,j). -/
def sumC (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) (i : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  ∑ j ∈ Finset.range (mk.N (X i ω)), mk.C (X i ω) j

/-- Sum of the squared weights of node `i`: Σ_{j ≤ 𝓝_i} 𝓒²_(i,j). -/
def sumC2 (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) (i : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  ∑ j ∈ Finset.range (mk.N (X i ω)), mk.C (X i ω) j ^ 2

/-- ρ*₁ = E[Σ_{i ≤ 𝓝_∅} 𝓒_i]. -/
noncomputable def rho1star (P : Measure Ω) (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) : ℝ :=
  ∫ ω, sumC mk X [] ω ∂P

/-- ρ₁ = E[Σ_{i ≤ 𝓝₁} 𝓒_(1,i)]. -/
noncomputable def rho1 (P : Measure Ω) (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) : ℝ :=
  ∫ ω, sumC mk X [0] ω ∂P

/-- ρ*₂ = E[Σ_{i ≤ 𝓝_∅} 𝓒²_i]. -/
noncomputable def rho2star (P : Measure Ω) (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) : ℝ :=
  ∫ ω, sumC2 mk X [] ω ∂P

/-- 𝓨_i = E[𝓦_i^(0) | 𝓧_i] for a signal family `sig i k ω` (an a.e.-defined function of ω). -/
noncomputable def condMeanSig (P : Measure Ω) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) (sig : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ → Ω → ℝ)
    (i : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label) : Ω → ℝ :=
  P[sig i 0 | MeasurableSpace.comap (X i) inferInstance]

/-- 𝓥_i = Var(𝓦_i^(0) | 𝓧_i) for a signal family `sig i k ω` (an a.e.-defined function of ω). -/
noncomputable def condVarSig (P : Measure Ω) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) (sig : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ → Ω → ℝ)
    (i : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label) : Ω → ℝ :=
  Var[sig i 0; P | MeasurableSpace.comap (X i) inferInstance]

/-- Limiting opinion of node `i` for the general recursion (1)/(8) with signals `sig`:
Σ_{s ≥ 0} (Δ^s 𝓦^(s))(i), with Δ of weights 𝓒 and self-weight 1 − c − d. -/
noncomputable def limOpinion (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) (sig : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ → Ω → ℝ)
    (c d : ℝ) (i : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  nodeOpinion (nAt mk X ω) (wAt mk X ω) (1 - c - d) (fun s j => sig j s ω) i

/-- Opinion of node `i` at time `k` of recursion (1) with 𝓡^(0) ≡ 0 and signals `sig`. -/
noncomputable def fwdOpinionAt (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M)
    (sig : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ → Ω → ℝ) (c d : ℝ) (k : ℕ) (i : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  fwdOpinion (nAt mk X ω) (wAt mk X ω) (1 - c - d) (fun s j => sig j s ω) k i

/-- 𝓜* of Proposition 6: root opinion of the general recursion (8) with the Section 5.1
signals 𝓦 = d𝓩 + 𝓠(c − Σ𝓒) (the appendix's 𝓡*). -/
noncomputable def Mstar (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) (U : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ → Ω → ℝ)
    (ζ : M → ℝ → ℝ) (c d : ℝ) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.rootOpinion (nAt mk X ω) (wAt mk X ω) (1 - c - d) (fun s i => DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.W mk X U ζ c d i s ω)

/-- 𝓡* of Proposition 6: root opinion of the no-memory recursion (9), with weights
𝓒/(c + d), no self term, and signals 𝓦/(c + d). -/
noncomputable def RstarNoMem (mk : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.MarkFns M) (X : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → Ω → M) (U : DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.Label → ℕ → Ω → ℝ)
    (ζ : M → ℝ → ℝ) (c d : ℝ) (ω : Ω) : ℝ :=
  DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.rootOpinion (nAt mk X ω) (fun i j => wAt mk X ω i j / (c + d)) 0
    (fun s i => DirectedOpinion.NoMemory.W mk X U ζ c d i s ω / (c + d))

end DirectedOpinion.Memory


